WEBVTT

00:00:03.649 --> 00:00:09.070
Before drawing anything, set the units in Model Settings.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:15.820
Unit name is the suffix shown
on every measurement. Type cm.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:23.450
Unit size says how long one model
unit is. One unit, one centimetre.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:31.480
Grid size is the snap spacing,
in units. Five gives a 5 cm grid.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:39.510
Good. Now move over the grid. The coloured
axes on the cursor show where it snaps.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:43.781
Start with the table top. Choose Rectangle.

00:00:43.831 --> 00:00:50.828
Click two grid points, 60 cm apart in each direction.

00:00:50.878 --> 00:00:58.778
Uh oh, nothing to snap to up in the
air. Press T to add an axis helper.

00:00:58.828 --> 00:01:04.489
Its blue axis points straight
up and snaps at every grid step.

00:01:04.539 --> 00:01:21.445
Push/Pull: pick the corner, then
a point one step up the helper.

00:01:21.495 --> 00:01:31.177
Nice! Make Object keeps this part
from merging with what we draw next.

00:01:31.227 --> 00:01:45.182
Now lift the top. Move: pick its
corner, then a point up the helper.

00:01:45.232 --> 00:01:54.288
Goooood. Next, one leg: a small
square under the corner of the top.

00:01:54.338 --> 00:02:08.728
Pull it up until the cursor snaps
to the corner underneath the top.

00:02:10.244 --> 00:02:19.678
Make it an object too, so all
four legs share one definition.

00:02:19.728 --> 00:02:33.839
Move Copy repeats it. Pick the leg's
corner, then a grid point 55 cm along.

00:02:33.889 --> 00:02:50.519
You can also type a distance. Pick a
start, aim, type 55 and press Enter.

00:02:50.909 --> 00:03:00.569
Niiiice! Clear Guides removes the
helper once it has done its job.

00:03:00.619 --> 00:03:06.519
Right-drag to orbit and check
the result from another side.

00:03:06.569 --> 00:03:16.626
Cool. That's the whole method: set units,
snap to the grid, climb with helpers.
